### 🟠 Major (strongly recommended)
- `evals/orchestration/tasks/t14-constraint-horizon/oracle.sh:5-6` — The new comment asserts "runner passes it as $1 — same contract as the other oracles," but this is **verifiably false** for every call site in the repo. `evals/orchestration/run-orchestration-eval.sh:309-311` invokes `bash oracle.sh` with **zero arguments**, having already `cd "$TEMP_REPO"` itself one line earlier (`run-orchestration-eval.sh:310`). The self-test harness does the same for every task it covers (`hooks/tests/orchestration-eval.test.sh:29,63,86,111,...` — all `bash oracle.sh` with no args, preceded by an explicit `cd`). `score.js` never shells out to `oracle.sh` at all (only reads `oracle_pass` from the JSON, `score.js:101`). I found no call site anywhere in the repo (including t10-t13, which have the identical pre-existing `if [ $# -ge 1 ]; then cd "$1"; fi` block, e.g. `t10-format-migrate/oracle.sh:6-8`, `t11-boundary-fix/oracle.sh:6-8`, `t12-cleanup-script/oracle.sh:6-8`) that ever passes `$1`. Consequence: (a) the added block is dead code — it does not fix whatever cd-related defect motivated this change, since the production/self-test call path already `cd`s before invoking `oracle.sh` with no args; (b) the false "contract" claim is a maintainability hazard — a future refactor of `run-orchestration-eval.sh` that trusts this comment (e.g. dropping its own `cd "$TEMP_REPO"` on the theory that "oracle.sh handles it via $1 like the others") would silently break oracle execution for **all 14** tasks, not just t14. Fix direction: correct the comment to state the actual contract (the runner already `cd`s into the temp repo before calling `oracle.sh` with no arguments; this guard exists only so `oracle.sh` can optionally be invoked standalone against an arbitrary path, matching the sibling oracles' style) — or remove the block if standalone invocation isn't an actual supported use case. If the original intent was to fix a real cd-related bug elsewhere, that bug is not addressed by this hunk and needs to be re-identified.

### 🟡 Minor (recommended)
- `evals/orchestration/tasks/t14-constraint-horizon/oracle.sh` (whole file) — t14 has **no self-test coverage** in `hooks/tests/orchestration-eval.test.sh` (only T1–T8 are exercised there; T9–T14 are absent — confirmed via grep, no `t9-`/`t10-`/…/`t14-` matches). This is a pre-existing gap, not introduced by this diff, but it means the change under review (and the t14 oracle generally) ships with zero automated verification that it still classifies pristine/fixed states correctly. Disclosing this as an uncovered bound rather than treating the diff as verified-by-tests. Fix direction: add a T14 pristine/fixed pair to `orchestration-eval.test.sh` following the T1-T8 pattern.

